- **Measured**: 104 yards on 13 hulls. Before, all 104 stood past the two radii and 56 bunts reached into the pole, up to 0.25 m. After, all 104 at the two radii to 7 mm, no roll inside any pole, every roll above and touching its yard. PROOF A was exactly 264 problems under the three furled rules and nothing else. Final audit: 33 hulls, 0 problems on both servers.
- **Frames**: the opening full ratchet at the clean r258 HEAD was clean at all 65. After the push, shipwright-furled moved 4.47% and action-salamis 0.11%, both read and accepted with reasons. action-myeongnyang stayed under the gate.
- **Witnessed**: the 74 before and after at the frame's own camera. Before, a bare yard with the roll slung under it. After, the roll on the yard with the bunt standing before the mast.

**Not resolved**: the topgallant parrel witness r258 asked for. The Shipwright camera targets the hull's centre, so the URL's height did not aim it aloft. The handoff names this and suggests a capture-harness target or a Sea-view masthead crop for r260.

**Next round** opens with the full ratchet at the clean HEAD, then takes (0y³⁵), the lateen's and lug's rolls onto their yards by the same seat, or (0y³⁰), the truss's throw, or Endurance by looking. One memory note was saved on the audit runner's output shape.
