**Round 294 is live: Preussen's forecastle and poop now reach the ends of her hull.** I scored 9 of the 65 frames, so the other 56 are unchecked at this build. The change only affects Preussen, and the four control frames I ran on other ships and the globe stayed inside the gate.

August's second list has been finished since round 57, so I took the top carried item, the ends of Preussen's raised decks.

| Raised deck | Before | After | Anchor plate |
|---|---|---|---|
| Forecastle | 6.6 m | 12.78 m | 12.8 m |
| Poop | 10.0 m | 14.93 m | 14.9 ± 1.3 m |
| Midship bridge | 24.30 m | 24.30 m | 24.2 m |

- **Cause:** the builder placed these decks on a straight line while the hull's ends rake, so the forecastle started 6.2 m behind the stem and the poop stopped 4.8 m short of the stern. Round 293's proposed fix, moving only the record, would have put the forecastle's break 2.2 m off the plate, so the builder and record changed together.
